      "content": "it's just... everything feels so staged, like i'm playing a part in a play that should've ended chapters ago. the help you're talking about feels so loud and jarring against the quietness of the house. don't you see the beauty in it? the way the fog doesn't demand anything, doesn't ask you to be better or stronger... it just offers to swallow the ache. there is something so much more honest about the silence than all this striving to stay.",
